  "question": "Does removing inherited binary-query and retinal-support restrictions expose useful safe singleton identity links?",
  "hypothesis": "Among any number of free high same-class detections, exactly one ordinary predicted-IoU>=0.2 candidate may identify a newly native-confirmed fragment. The optional reverse constant-velocity check may reject foreign links. Native physical outputs never change.",
  "literature": [
    {
